      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6319834cd042b344ab56243e",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While I don't really care for the underage users reasoning (since VRChat isn't exactly facilitating the purchase of alcohol) I do think the concerns toward those with drinking problems, such as those who are trying to quit, do not need drinking stuck in their face in this way.\nEDIT: Yeah no I agree with Chirping_Cat above me now that someone's laid out the argument, tag should stay.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "631d1c6fc95d8944d1ea4da9",
      "author": {
        "_id": "618fa6ccbfca2a69d13f829c",
        "alias": "Proposed Crayfish",
        "aliasID": "65c291beed6eefce4cf7f963",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/7d69d5303fd2d5f060f58f5a01abeff7.png",
        "created": "2021-11-13T11:51:40.718Z",
        "name": "Chirping_Cat",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-09-10T23:23:27.134Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6319834cd042b344ab56243e",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 18
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am afraid I have to disagree with the OP on this suggestion, which I can only describe as well-meaning symbolism that could harm those with drinking-related problems. The word “Drinking” on a page doesn’t make people want to drink any more than any other background pressure they face daily. The word drinking and drinking-related themes are everywhere in movies, TV shows, advertising across all mediums, office culture and how we celebrate big occasions or holidays as a society, or the passive knowledge that pubs and clubs exist. Yes, humanity is drenched in alcohol-related culture, and it takes a level of perseverance not to partake in that.\nHowever, people are more likely to succumb to drinking alcohol when they find themselves (often inadvertently) in social situations where others consume alcohol. Alcoholics generally try to avoid being in these situations or try to be around friends they can trust to support them. But they need to foresee the situation as risky to avoid it, like they might avoid entering a pub or bottleshop. That foresight comes from simple, clear messaging, and in the case of VRChat drinking-oriented worlds, that messaging takes the form of accurate world tagging and descriptions. A drinking-oriented world is likely to have people drinking within it, and knowing it’s that type of world allows you to avoid that situation —common sense.\nNow, the default search terms represent a new meta for world SEO and tagging because no one likes typing in VR. Hence, as its refined (Read: Non-random positioning) players will increasingly use that functionality, and world creators will focus on ensuring their worlds fit into at least one of the predefined terms. By having the term ‘Drinking’ as a default search term, world creators are encouraged to clearly describe and tag their worlds as such whilst not feeling forced to have their world show up under other search terms to be seen. A failure to accommodate the existence of drinking-oriented worlds in the new search meta will likely result in those world creators simply tagging their world with “the next best tag” to fit somewhere else in the default search terms. This type of search gaming will obscure drinking worlds, make it harder for alcoholics to know if heavy drinking is likely to occur in worlds they’re about to enter, and increase their exposure to those drinking-related world listings in other default search terms. Its easy to forsee the 'Social' default search term becoming the home of all drinking worlds if this suggestion is adopted, and making it more challenging for alcoholics to exercise informed choice is the last thing anyone wants because it will foreseeably increase the occurrences of alcoholics being put in risky situations. Hence, this suggestion may one day cost a life, using the parlance of the OP. \nWhile I respect the OP’s desire to be helpful, it is painfully apparent that they have never experienced alcoholism, which in fairness, does take many forms.\nFinally, the ‘think of the children’ remarks need to be taken with a grain of salt as they could easily apply to the Love, Romance, Dating, Bar, Clubs, Trippy, Psycedelic, Battle and Shooter default search terms as they could be construed (based upon the OP’s twisted logic, which I profoundly disagree with) as encouraging potentially unsafe online dating, drinking, drug use and gun violence respectively.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
